      "content": "For heavy industrial loads in a system like your Rotterdam facility, prioritize a low center of gravity by ensuring the heaviest items are at the bottom of every pallet stack. Implement interlocking patterns by staggering beams between adjacent pallets so that the loads lock together tightly without relying solely on gravity to hold the rack upright. Before finalizing your layout, conduct a thorough structural calculation specific to the beam spacing and lateral loads unique to your local conditions in Rotterdam. This combination of vertical weight distribution and lateral interlocking is essential for preventing instability under dynamic loading.",
