    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I get the vibration thing, but we've had cases where everything is perfectly level and stable, and then suddenly a single pallet just... shifts. It's almost like something nudged it. We're trying to figure out if it's just microscopic structural flaws or if there's something else we're missing regarding how these loads interact when they're packed so tightly. Is there anything else that could cause that kind of \"random\" movement?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
